# WireOS Git Submodule Workflow

This project uses **nested Git submodules**. Before any commit/push task, read:

`docs/GIT_SUBMODULE_WORKFLOW.md`

## Required branch

`xiaozhi-wireos-save-2026-07-14`

- Applies to: `wire-os`, `anki/victor`, `anki/victor/EXTERNALS`, `anki/wired`, `anki/vic-cloudless`
- Always push that branch only
- Never push/checkout/merge/rebase onto `main` or `master` unless the user explicitly asks
- If a WireOS repo is on another branch, stop and report — do not auto-checkout

## Owned repos (haryken)

| Path | Origin |
|------|--------|
| `.` (wire-os) | `git@github.com:haryken/wire-os.git` |
| `anki/victor` | `git@github.com:haryken/wire-os-victor.git` |
| `anki/victor/EXTERNALS` | `git@github.com:haryken/wire-os-externals.git` |
| `anki/wired` | `git@github.com:haryken/wired.git` |
| `anki/vic-cloudless` | `git@github.com:haryken/vic-cloudless.git` |

## Community deps — do not touch unless asked

`external/purplpkg`, `poky/bitbake`, `poky/meta-openembedded`, `poky/openembedded-core`

If dirty: report only. No commit/push/reset/clean/discard.

## Commit/push order (inside → outside)

- EXTERNALS changes: `EXTERNALS` → `victor` → `wire-os`
- wired changes: `wired` → `wire-os`
- vic-cloudless changes: `vic-cloudless` → `wire-os`
- Multiple children: EXTERNALS → victor → wired → vic-cloudless → **wire-os last**

Parent stores submodule **SHA pointers**, not full child trees. Push the child before committing the parent pointer.

## Inspect before staging

When the user asks to commit/push/save to GitHub:

1. Inspect parent + `git submodule foreach --recursive` status/branch/remote
2. Do **not** blindly `git add .`
3. Stage only inspected, appropriate files (source/config/needed assets/pointers)
4. Ask about unclear binaries, secrets, large/temp files
5. Never force-push; never rewrite history for LFS/size issues without asking

## After push

Report SHAs, branches, remotes, updated pointers, remaining dirty/untracked state, and any errors.
